        <detaileddescription>
<para>Some notes (SKM):</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Since PARDISO is written in C, extern &quot;C&quot; declarations are needed for MKL functions. For example</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>good news: PARDISO is free for academic user, just register and download</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>parameters are rather similar to those used by SAMG, so much of the code can be copied from SAMG_Solver.cpp</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++ examples in mklroot\solverc\source\ directory</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Intel MKL PARDISO is a direct sparse solver based on Parallel Direct Sparse <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_solver" kindref="compound">Solver</ref> PARDISO*), an iterative sparse solver, and supporting sparse BLAS (level 1, 2, and 3) routines for solving sparse systems of equations, as well as a distributed version of Intel MKL PARDISO solver provided for use on clusters.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>See PARDISO User&apos;s Guide and <ulink url="http://www.pardiso-project.org">http://www.pardiso-project.org</ulink> (Olaf Schenk, supercomputer center, Mano, Lugano)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>PARDISO is defined in MKL_DOMAIN_PARDISO of the mkl.h header file.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>is there another sparse direct solver? - mkl_dss.h</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>solver uses LaPack / libmkl_lapack.dylib </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
